{
  "dom_id": "step-e5784",
  "name": "Example: Factoring a Sum of Squares",
  "problem": "Factor $m^2 + 16n^2.$",
  "worked_solution": "To factor a sum of squares, we first write it as a difference. Then, we rewrite the second term using $\\textrm{i}^2 = -1.$ Finally, we factor as a difference of squares.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}^{2}+16{n}^{2} & ={m}^{2}-(-16{n}^{2}) \\\\  & ={m}^{2}-(16\\,{\\text{i}}^{2}{n}^{2}) \\\\  & ={m}^{2}-({4}^{2}{\\text{i}}^{2}{n}^{2}) \\\\  & ={m}^{2}-{(4\\text{i}n)}^{2} \\\\  & =(m+4\\text{i}n)(m-4\\text{i}n).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "result": null,
